- op: create  # 53dc
  at: '2026-08-23T17:46:59Z'  # 53dc
  by: agent  # 53dc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 53dc
  clock: 1  # 53dc
  nonce: 53dc  # 53dc
  data:  # 53dc
    kind: invariant  # 53dc
    title: "module_attr_ref in _CALL_SITE_EDGE_TYPES makes use-statements and return-type annotations count as call sites, so a zero-dependency crate is withheld as inconclusive naming its own stdlib"  # 53dc
    status: violated  # 53dc
    priority: 1  # 53dc
    parent:  # 53dc
    tags:  # 53dc
    - io_boundary  # 53dc
    - verify_claims  # 53dc
    - rust  # 53dc
    - false_inconclusive  # 53dc
    isbefore: []  # 53dc
    duplicate_of: []  # 53dc
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 53dc
    pr_ref:  # 53dc
    description: "MEASURED 2026-08-23 on an authored two-arm Rust fixture (no build.rs, no\ndependencies, so arm B never executes untrusted code):\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rust_fidelity_probe_08232026/.\n\nSYMPTOM. verify-claims returns inconclusive for net_send and fs_write on a\ncrate with ZERO dependencies, reporting that \"the analysis makes calls into 3\nmodule(s) that the I/O catalog could not classify (std, std.io, std.net)\".\nThose are the Rust standard library, and rust.yaml catalogues them explicitly\n(std::net::UdpSocket, std::io::Write, std::fs).\n\nMECHANISM, read from the emitted edge set. _CALL_SITE_EDGE_TYPES\n(verify_claims.py) is call_family_edge_types() UNION {\"module_attr_ref\"}. In\nthis fixture ALL EIGHT module_attr_ref edges are non-calls:\n  * 5 originate at the FILE node (rust:src/lib.rs:1-1:file:file) and are the\n    attribute-chain decomposition of three `use` statements;\n  * 3 originate at function nodes and are the `std::io::Result<...>` RETURN\n    TYPE annotations.\nZero are call sites. The docstring on _external_call_sites, one screen below\nthe constant, states the set \"deliberately exclud[es] imports (see that\nconstant)\" because an import performs no I/O and the catalog classifies CALL\nSITES.\n\nTHIS IS A RECURRENCE, NOT A NEW BUG. INV-fibis's own 2026-08-09 entry records\nthe identical error being found and fixed once already: the first draft of the\nuncatalogued-module gate \"counted imports edges -- 231 of the 258 modules it\nreported on poetry\". The exclusion was implemented against the `imports` edge\nTYPE, so the same fact re-entered through a different edge type.\n\nCONSEQUENCE. The gate cannot distinguish \"this repo calls into a third-party\nmodule I cannot classify\" from \"this repo has a use statement\". On a fixture\nwith no dependencies at all, the second alone is enough to withhold a verdict.\nThe direction is fail-safe (inconclusive, not confirmed), so this is a\nPRECISION defect in the gate, not a false-confirm -- but it makes the\ninconclusive verdict unreadable, and the reported module list actively\nmisleading.\n\nNOT MEASURED: how many modules on a real repo's inconclusive list are\nimport-derived rather than call-derived, in any language. The poetry figure\nabove (231/258) is for the ALREADY-FIXED imports path, not for this one."  # 53dc
    fields:  # 53dc
      statement: "The uncatalogued-module coverage gate must adjudicate CALL SITES only: a module named solely by an import or a type annotation performs no I/O and must not withhold a boundary verdict."  # 53dc
      root_cause: "_CALL_SITE_EDGE_TYPES (packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/verify_claims.py:1618) unions module_attr_ref onto the call family. module_attr_ref is emitted for use-statement attribute chains and for return-type annotations, neither of which is a call. The imports exclusion the adjacent docstring describes is implemented against the imports edge TYPE, so the same fact re-enters through module_attr_ref."  # 53dc
- op: discuss  # d1cd
  at: '2026-08-24T03:23:09Z'  # d1cd
  by: agent  # d1cd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d1cd
  clock: 2  # d1cd
  nonce: d1cd  # d1cd
  message: "ROOT CAUSE CORRECTED AFTER READING THE PRODUCER. The symptom in the description\nreproduces exactly as filed. The MECHANISM this item named -- module_attr_ref\nbeing a member of _CALL_SITE_EDGE_TYPES -- is NOT the root cause, and the fix\nit implies is measurably the WORSE of the two available.\n\nWHAT THE EDGES ACTUALLY ARE, from the shared emitter (analyze/base.py\nemit_module_attribute_refs, scoped_path=True) run directly on an authored\nfixture:\n\n  use std::fs;                                 -> module_attr_ref  ARTIFACT\n  use std::net::UdpSocket;                     -> module_attr_ref  ARTIFACT (x2)\n  fn f() -> std::io::Result<String>            -> module_attr_ref  ARTIFACT\n  std::env::consts::OS                         -> module_attr_ref  GENUINE (x3)\n\n5 of 8 on the filed fixture are producer artifacts. The emitter walks every\n`scoped_identifier` not in callee position and calls it an attribute read; a\n`use` path and a return-type path are both scoped_identifiers.\n\nTHE DUPLICATE HOME, which is the actual defect and is LIVE.md rule 7. The SAME\nthree `use` statements are ALREADY emitted as `imports` edges in the same run:\n\n  imports          rust:std::fs:0-0:module:external_symbol\n  module_attr_ref  rust:std:0-0:std.fs:external_symbol\n\nOne fact, two edge families, two spellings. The gate deliberately excludes the\n`imports` family because an import performs no I/O -- and the identical fact\nre-enters through the second family. That is verbatim the recurrence INV-fibis\nrecorded on 2026-08-09 (\"the exclusion was implemented against the imports edge\nTYPE, so the same fact re-entered\"), and it is a PRODUCER duplicate, not a\nconsumer set-membership question.\n\nMEASURED PRICE OF THE CONSUMER FIX THIS ITEM PROPOSED. On hypergumbo's own\ntree (.hypergumbo/self-analysis.json, 145,727 edges, 12 catalogued languages):\n\n  module_attr_ref edges                          1,368\n  ... reaching _external_call_sites               1,368  (100%)\n  ALL edges reaching _external_call_sites        32,654  (module_attr_ref = 4.2%)\n  uncatalogued module list, as shipped               99\n  uncatalogued module list, module_attr_ref dropped  91\n  modules ONLY module_attr_ref reports                 8\n      builtins, google, mypy, navigator,\n      sentence_transformers, std, std.cmp, tokenizers\n\nOnly `std` and `std.cmp` are the artifacts. The other six are GENUINE\nthird-party attribute reads on uncatalogued modules -- exactly the\nclassification opportunity the gate exists to protect, and exactly what the\ncatalogues' `attributes:` sections are for (os.environ, System.out, std::cout).\nSo dropping module_attr_ref from _CALL_SITE_EDGE_TYPES would delete six real\ndisclosures to remove two artifacts. Fixing the producer removes the artifacts\nand costs none of the six.\n\nLANGUAGE ANALOGUES CHECKED, not assumed. The defect is present in BOTH\nscoped_path=True languages and absent elsewhere:\n  rust  `use std::fs;`      and `-> std::io::Result<_>`  -> both emitted\n  cpp   `using std::string;` and `std::string f(int)`    -> both emitted\n  python `import os` and `def f(p: os.PathLike) -> os.PathLike` -> NEITHER\n         emitted (py.py's own helper is correct). Genuine reads (os.environ,\n         std::cout) are emitted in all three.\nSo the fix belongs in the shared emitter's scoped_path branch -- one home,\nboth languages -- and needs a per-language skip-context tuple beside the\nnode_kinds / object_field_names tuples it already takes. Measured ancestor\nchains give an exact discriminator: an artifact's first non-node_kinds ancestor\nis `use_declaration` / `using_declaration` (import) or\n`scoped_type_identifier` / `generic_type` / `function_definition` (type\nposition); a genuine read's is `block` / `binary_expression`.\n\nSECOND, INDEPENDENT CAUSE FOUND AND FILED SEPARATELY rather than folded in\nhere: rust.yaml declares ZERO `module_completeness` entries, so\nmodule_io_is_enumerated returns False for EVERY Rust module in BOTH spellings\n(std, std::io, std.io, std::net, std.net, std::fs, std.fs, std::env, std.env\n-- all False). Step (2) of the gate can therefore never pass for Rust, and any\nstd call the catalogue has no row for is reported as uncatalogued even after\nthe producer is fixed. The filed repro closes on the producer fix alone\n(measured: uncatalogued list goes ['std','std.io','std.net'] -> [] with the\nmodule_attr_ref edges removed), but the class does not.\n\nTHIRD DEFECT, ALSO FILED SEPARATELY: the left-recursive prefix walk emits one\nedge per nesting depth, so ONE genuine read `std::env::consts::OS` emits three\nedges and at most one can ever match a catalogue row. The other two are\nreported as uncatalogued modules. Verified on the shipped CLI: a crate whose\nonly scoped read is that genuine one still returns inconclusive naming\n\"std, std.env.consts, std.net\".\n\nSTATUS STAYS violated. Nothing has been fixed yet; this entry corrects the\nmechanism so the fix lands in the right place."  # d1cd
