- op: discuss  # 3633
  at: '2026-08-26T20:13:04Z'  # 3633
  by: agent  # 3633
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3633
  clock: 10  # 3633
  nonce: '3633'  # 3633
  message: "REOPENING 2026-08-26. THE FIX WAS INCOMPLETE AND THE CLOSURE PROVES ONLY THAT\nTHE REPRO PASSED, NOT THAT THE STATEMENT HOLDS.\n\nThis item's statement: \"a module named solely by an import or a type annotation\nperforms no I/O and must not withhold a boundary verdict.\" That is ratified and\nunchanged. What shipped covers ONE rust `use` form.\n\nMEASURED on merged dev, encrypted-dns-server (rust+toml only). The skip tuple is\n(\"use_declaration\", \"scoped_type_identifier\", \"generic_type\"), and\n`_scoped_context_kind` walks past ancestors that are THEMSELVES scoped nodes --\nso it reports the first NON-scoped ancestor. For a braced use, that ancestor is\nan inner structural node of the use declaration, not its context:\n\n  use std::path::Path;                        ctx=use_declaration     SKIPPED\n  use std::io::{BufRead, BufReader};          ctx=scoped_use_list     LEAKS\n  use std::io::{self, Write};                 ctx=scoped_use_list     LEAKS\n  use std::io::*;                             ctx=use_wildcard        LEAKS\n  use std::io::Write as W;                    ctx=use_as_clause       LEAKS\n  use std::collections::{hash_map::Entry, C}; ctx=use_list            LEAKS\n\nFIVE FORMS, verified by parsing each with tree-sitter-rust and calling the\nproduction `_scoped_context_kind` directly, not by reading the grammar.\n\nTHE CONSEQUENCE IS A PERMANENT CEILING, not a stray edge. A braced\n`use std::net::{...}` emits a module_attr_ref whose MODULE SLOT is bare `std` --\nthe crate root. `std` can never carry `module_completeness: complete` (that\nwould assert every I/O primitive in the entire standard library is enumerated),\nso every rust repository carries an entry the uncatalogued-module gate can never\nclear, no matter how many modules WI-lutuh enumerates. Present in ALL FIVE rust\nrepos of the WI-lutuh sample; re-confirmed by recomputing\n`_uncatalogued_external_modules` directly on the cached surveys for\nencrypted-dns-server (32 uncatalogued, 16 rust stdlib, `std` among them) and\nripgrep (25 / 17, same).\n\nAll 17 bare-`std` edges on that repo are `module_attr_ref`. ZERO are `calls`.\n\nDOCUMENTED NOWHERE: `scoped_use_list` appears in no source file, no ADR, no spec\nsection, no playbook and no tracker item. This thread never considered braced,\nnested, wildcard or `as` forms. Exactly one commit ever touched the skip tuple\n(254a69e332, this item's own fix).\n\nRULED (agent, reversible, reasoning here): complete THIS item rather than filing\na new invariant -- the statement already covers every leaking form. Fix in the\nLANGUAGE files, because the shared walker is language-agnostic and must not\nlearn rust's grammar. Generalize via a FORM-ENUMERATION TEST over every use\nform, WITH A NEGATIVE CONTROL asserting a genuine expression-position read still\nemits -- without it the skip tuple could grow until the emitter is dead and\nevery `attributes:` catalogue row silently unreachable, which no other test\nwould notice. Do NOT special-case `std` at the gate: that suppresses a\ndisclosure whose producer is broken, while looking fixed.\n\nDIRECTION OF RISK, stated because it cuts the wrong way by default: removing\nthese edges removes WITHHOLDING, which produces MORE clean verdicts -- normally\nthe direction to scrutinize. It is safe here only because a `use` declaration\nperforms no I/O by construction and is already recorded as an `imports` edge the\ngate deliberately excludes. That is this item's own ratified reasoning.\n\nNOT FOLDED IN, deliberately: a scoped path in CALLEE position\n(`std::process::exit(1)`) also emits a prefix module_attr_ref. That is prefix\ncollateral of a real call, a different mechanism, partly handled by INV-hukuf's\nsibling test. Folding it here would repeat the error being corrected --\nresolving a broad statement against a narrow repro.\n\nTHE TRANSFERABLE LESSON: A CLOSURE CAN SATISFY THE REPRO AND NOT THE STATEMENT.\nWhen closing, ask what the statement covers that the fixture CANNOT REACH."  # 3633
